  "A0100": "A0100 most plausibly seeks to reduce exposure after launching while preserving survival against the closing opposing formation by breaking sharply to the east and continuing its descent, given its missile count decrease as the sustained rightward turn begins; the maneuver also coincides with a newly appearing opposing missile, though evasion cannot be confirmed.",
  "A0200": "A0200 most plausibly seeks to maintain the head-on attack and keep closing for continued missile employment by accelerating northward with only modest lateral adjustment and a sustained descent, given its missile expenditure during the approach while both opposing aircraft remain active and continue converging."
