{
  "A0100": "A0100 most plausibly seeks to reduce exposure while its already-launched missile continues toward the opposing formation by making a sustained rightward break from the northward approach, creating lateral separation as opposing missiles descend southward from ahead; the aircraft remains alive while its eastward displacement grows markedly.",
  "A0200": "A0200 most plausibly seeks to preserve an attacking approach and then obtain lateral separation as the engagement develops, initially continuing north toward the opposing aircraft while its missile is in flight before turning right late in the window; opposing missiles remain on southbound trajectories and the aircraft continues descending and accelerating."
}

{
  "A0100": "A0100 most plausibly seeks to preserve a fast, laterally separated support position while an existing missile engagement develops by holding its eastbound, level course and increasing speed; it remains well south of the opposing aircraft and does not materially alter course when A0200’s missile and B0200 disappear.",
  "A0200": "A0200 most plausibly seeks a favorable crossing or attack position against the opposing formation by accelerating through a sustained right turn and descent, then continuing to reposition after the existing A02002 missile is removed concurrently with B0200 becoming inactive; the later left corrections suggest geometry adjustment rather than simple straight-line pursuit."
}

{
  "A0100": "A0100 most plausibly seeks to reduce exposure and create lateral separation from a nearby missile track by turning sharply left after sustained eastward flight, then continuing northward at high altitude; this change begins as B01002 disappears after traversing nearby, although removal does not establish a hit or confirmed targeting.",
  "A0200": "A0200 most plausibly seeks to survive an approaching missile while preserving a usable attack position by descending and executing a prolonged left-turning break; B01001 advances from the northwest toward its changing vicinity throughout the window, while the aircraft’s heading and altitude shift substantially, with no confirmed missile outcome."
}

{
  "A0100": "A0100 most plausibly seeks to reduce exposure after achieving a launch opportunity by descending through a sustained left turn, expending its remaining missile, and then bending back right to create lateral separation; the ammunition decrease and missile appearance support a launch, while the continued break leaves no basis for claiming a hit.",
  "A0200": "A0200 most plausibly seeks to escape the close B0100–missile geometry by maintaining speed while turning its flight path progressively northward and separating laterally from the opposing track; the nearby B missile remains west of it throughout, and the aircraft continues this evasive-looking repositioning even after B0100 becomes inactive."
}
